************ SIMULATIONS WITH ARGON ******************

Simulations contained the following numbers of atoms: 343, 512, 729, 1000

###########################################################################
Time-step was equal to 2 fs
Cut-off was 6 Å
Integrator was leapfrog
Temperature was 120 K with the coupling constant equal to 0.5 ps
The algorithm for thermostat was Velocity Rescale
Barostat was Berendsen with the coupling constant 10 ps
Pressure was 1 atm
Pressure coupling scheme was isotropic (equal in all 3 directions)

###########################################################################
Values for SANS profiles were computed on the interval of 2.5-3 ns.
The total duration of each simulation was 3 ns.

###########################################################################
Files with sq are for S(q), pr are for G(r). Numbers stand for simulations with the same settings.

###########################################################################
FIles named as CONV_*.dat are values to analyze the convergence of each simulations. 
The first column is the time in ps, the second one is the E_tot - total energy during the whole simulation in kJ/mol,
the second column is the temperature in K, and the last one is the size of the box in X-direction in nm.
